From 29e0793316030aaa3c585dc8a6259f627b4b558d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: toneloc <3665696+toneloc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:52:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add ExternalFundingSigner hook for externally held channel
 funding keys

Introduces `signer::NodeChannelSigner`, a wrapper around LDK's
`InMemorySigner` that routes the channel funding key (pubkey and all
signatures made with it: commitment, closing, keyed anchor, channel
announcement, splice shared input) to a pluggable
`signer::ExternalFundingSigner`. All other channel keys stay locally
derived. `Builder::set_external_funding_signer` enables it.

Signers are restored via `SignerProvider::derive_channel_signer`, so no
serialization changes are needed. Adds a `_test_utils` feature mirroring
lightning's for the test-only signer method.

AI tooling disclosure: written with Claude Code assistance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
